<title>UK: EU pact offers little cheer to mark-analysts.</title>
<headline>EU pact offers little cheer to mark-analysts.</headline>
<byline>Abigail Levene</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The mark found its feet on Monday after sliding on the unveiling of the EU budget stability pact, but analysts saw little in the accord to restore it to health.</p>
<p>The pact approved strict budget deficit limits for monetary union participants, but allowed for a political judgement on whether to levy fines on those who overspend.</p>
<p>&quot;The very fact we reach a stability agreement of any kind is mark-negative and positive for the other EMS currencies, simply because it keeps the momentum behind EMU relatively strong,&quot; said Joe Prendergast, currency strategist at Merrill Lynch.</p>
</text>
